        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "e9d37267-c249-5fc2-bea8-bc218ff1407b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Margarita Lozano, Claude Berri, Luis Buñuel, Sergio Leone, Pier Paolo Pasolini, Taviani brothers, Nanni Moretti, Marcel Pagnol, Carmelo Gómez, Iciar Bollain, Francisco Algora\n- Films: Viridiana, A Fistful of Dollars, Pigsty, The Night of the Shooting Stars, Kaos, Good Morning Babylon, La messa è finita, Jean de Florette, Manon of the Spring, Manon des Sources, Nos miran, The Chicken\n\nFacts:\n- In 1961, Margarita Lozano worked with Luis Buñuel in \"Viridiana\".\n- In 1964, Margarita Lozano worked with Sergio Leone in \"A Fistful of Dollars\".\n- In 1965, Claude Berri directed the French short comedy film \"The Chicken\" (French: \"Le Poulet\").\n- In 1969, Margarita Lozano worked with Pier Paolo Pasolini in \"Pigsty\".\n- In 1982, Margarita Lozano worked with the Taviani brothers in \"The Night of the Shooting Stars\".\n- In 1984, Margarita Lozano worked with the Taviani brothers in \"Kaos\".\n- In 1986, \"Manon des Sources\" is a French-language film directed by Claude Berri.\n- In 1986, \"Manon des Sources\" was the second of two films adapted from Marcel Pagnol's 1966 two-volume novel, which he wrote from his own earlier film of the same title.\n- In 1986, Claude Berri's diptych included \"Jean de Florette\" and \"Manon of the Spring\", and Margarita Lozano appeared in both films.\n- In 1985, Margarita Lozano worked with Nanni Moretti in \"La messa è finita\".\n- In 1987, Margarita Lozano worked with the Taviani brothers in \"Good Morning Babylon\".\n- \"Nos miran\" is a thriller starring Carmelo Gómez with Iciar Bollain, Margarita Lozano, and Francisco Algora.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
